    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">1909.00155_rag::chunk_022</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">1909.00155_rag::chunk_020</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">To design a GNN accelerator, we analyzed several GNN benchmarks (Section V) and observed that the operations required</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">an architecture for efcient acceleration of GNN-based inference. To the best of our knowledge, this is the rst architecture for accelerating GNNs.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">the vertex property dimension variation is of vital importance to a general GNN accelerator design.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">architecture for efcient acceleration of GNN-based inference. To the best of our knowledge, this is the rst architecture for accelerating GNNs.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The average throughput of EnGN is 3265.87 GOP/s which achieves 79.7% of the peak throughput</hasEvidenceText>
  </rdf:Description>
