    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The whole GNN inference can thus be viewed as two separated phases: Aggregation and Combination .</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">a ( k + 1 ) v is the aggregation results through collecting neighbors information ( e.g. , node embeddings)</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">aggregation of node a , b , c , d , and e would load the embeddings of 15 nodes in total and most of these loads are repeated</hasEvidenceText>
  </rdf:Description>
